experiment: leverprobe
  instrument        leverprobe   trial seed 0000000001353929   2000 trials
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  question          `blockanchor` says freezing the UPPER half of F1 costs 53%
                    of the lesson and the LOWER half 9%. My leverage law was
                    FITTED to three one-neuron costs and FAILS the two
                    half-block costs from the same run: it predicts a ratio of
                    3.48 where 5.89 was measured, and no centroid position
                    reaches 5.89 (the maximum over all v is 4.31).
  what is measured  the two quantities that law ASSUMED -- the centroid's own
                    position and the per-neuron weights -- and, the point of
                    the run, how much each neuron's rate actually MOVES while
                    the lesson is learned. That needs no fitted constant.
  the prior         `stageprobe` says IP drives every neuron toward the SAME
                    rate, which flattens exactly this profile. A FLAT answer
                    here is the expected one and it REFUSES the rate account
                    as well as the position account.

  PRE-REGISTERED, written before the run
    primary     share of total |rate change| in the UPPER half (k=7..13),
                first third of teaching to last, taught arm.
      >= 0.75 and >= 2 SE above the `quiet` arm -> THE LESSON IS CARRIED BY
                THE UPPER HALF. Explains 53-vs-9 with no fitted law, and
                REPLACES the leverage account rather than repairing it.
      0.42..0.58                                -> REFUSED. Both halves move
                alike, so neither position nor rate explains the asymmetry
                and the cause is downstream of this profile.
      anything else                             -> report the number, no
                verdict. This is the 2-3 SE band where a hypothesis is not a
                finding.
    secondary   the centroid's MEASURED position, against the 0.299 the fit
                assumed. A measurement, not a gate.
    refusals    the group must be 14 neurons, the taught arm must reproduce
                `blockanchor`'s b0 lesson (+0.1676, accept 0.10..0.24), and
                pool_beta must be 1.0 or the centroid column is not the
                readout's. Any of these failing means this run is not
                measuring the creature those costs came from.

